From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Launcher3: the home screen goes in the file the image reads

The home screen came up with the browser alone, in a cell nobody would have put
it in, on a device whose layout had been written out in full
("依然「首页」只有浏览器，且位置不对", 2026-10-20, V59 on the device). The
layout was right both times. The file it was written in is one this image never
reads, and it took reading the built APK back to see that.

Launcher3 chooses the file: InvariantDeviceProfile measures the screen in dp,
keeps the nearest entries of res/xml/device_profiles.xml and takes
defaultLayoutId from the nearest one. But the image builds **Launcher3Go**, and
go/res/xml/device_profiles.xml replaces that whole file with one entry -- "Go
Device", 4 by 4, defaultLayoutId="@xml/default_workspace_4x4". With one entry
the dp of this screen decide nothing: it is the nearest of one. And
default_workspace_4x4.xml opens with

    <include launcher:workspace="@xml/dw_phone_hotseat" />

a dialer, messages, a camera and the market. This device has none of those, so
one entry of the file resolved -- the browser, in hotseat cell 3 -- and that
was the home screen. 0010 put the layout in default_workspace_5x6.xml and the
home screen stayed empty; 0011 made the database seed again and it came up with
that hotseat. Neither had anything to do with the eleven profiles of the base
res/xml/device_profiles.xml, which was the file this port kept editing.

So: the layout is default_workspace_pw3.xml, the Go profile names it, and the
base 5x6 file goes back to what AOSP has, since nothing here reads it. One
layout, named once, in the one table the image compiles. Which bucket of AOSP's
dp table this screen would fall into is then not a thing this port has an
opinion about, and neither is the status bar's height.

Verified on the built image rather than reasoned about: `aapt d xmltree
Launcher3Go.apk res/xml/device_profiles.xml` has one defaultLayoutId, and it is
the resource id of default_workspace_pw3.

The grid stays Go's: 4 columns, 4 rows, icons of 60dp. Four applications in
four columns is what the layout wants; what icon size a 1072 by 1448 panel
wants is a separate question with its own measurements, and so is the hotseat,
which this layout leaves empty.

SCHEMA_VERSION moves to 29 with it. loadDefaultFavoritesIfNecessary() fills a
database that was just created and nothing re-reads the layout afterwards, so a
release that changes what the first open shows -- the layout, or the profile
entry that names it -- has to move the version or it reaches nobody who already
has the system. 0011 moved it to 28 and the seed it produced was the wrong one;
this moves it again, and the layout file says so at the top of itself, which is
where somebody changing the home screen is reading.

diff --git a/go/res/xml/device_profiles.xml b/go/res/xml/device_profiles.xml
index 487c026..944886e 100644
--- a/go/res/xml/device_profiles.xml
+++ b/go/res/xml/device_profiles.xml
@@ -17,6 +17,13 @@
 
 <profiles xmlns:launcher="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto/com.android.launcher3" >
 
+    <!-- PW3: the layout is default_workspace_pw3.xml. AOSP's 4x4 layout begins
+         by including dw_phone_hotseat, whose dialer, messages, camera and
+         market are not on this device: one entry of it resolved, the browser,
+         and that was the whole home screen. This entry is the only one the
+         image reads, since go/res replaces the eleven of
+         res/xml/device_profiles.xml with it, so it is the only place the
+         layout can be named. -->
     <profile
         launcher:name="Go Device"
         launcher:minWidthDps="296"
@@ -27,7 +34,7 @@
         launcher:numFolderColumns="4"
         launcher:iconSize="60"
         launcher:iconTextSize="14.0"
-        launcher:defaultLayoutId="@xml/default_workspace_4x4"
+        launcher:defaultLayoutId="@xml/default_workspace_pw3"
         />
 
 </profiles>
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/res/raw/downgrade_schema.json b/res/raw/downgrade_schema.json
index 988978c..8e2894c 100644
--- a/res/raw/downgrade_schema.json
+++ b/res/raw/downgrade_schema.json
@@ -2,10 +2,11 @@
   // Note: Comments are not supported in JSON schema, but android parser is lenient.
 
   // Maximum DB version supported by this schema
-  "version" : 28,
+  "version" : 29,
 
-  // PW3: 28 only re-seeds the workspace, it does not change the tables, so a
-  // database written by it is read by 27 as it stands.
+  // PW3: 28 and 29 only re-seed the workspace, they do not change the tables,
+  // so a database written by either is read by the one before it as it stands.
+  "downgrade_to_28" : [],
   "downgrade_to_27" : [],
 
   // Downgrade from 27 to 26. Empty array indicates, the DB is compatible
