+<!-- PW3: the home screen of this device, and the only one it has.
+
+     Which file is read is the launcher's own decision and this project twice
+     wrote the layout into one it does not read. InvariantDeviceProfile takes
+     defaultLayoutId from the nearest entry of device_profiles.xml, and the
+     image builds Launcher3Go, whose go/res replaces that whole file with a
+     single entry: "Go Device", 4 by 4, naming default_workspace_4x4.xml. That
+     file begins by including dw_phone_hotseat, a dialer, messages, a camera
+     and the market, none of which are on this device; the browser was the one
+     entry of it that resolved, in hotseat cell 3. That was the home screen
+     ("依然「首页」只有浏览器，且位置不对", 2026-10-20, V59 on the device), and
+     before that an empty one (0010). Neither had anything to do with the dp of
+     this screen or with the table of eleven profiles in the base res/, which
+     the Go overlay replaces.
+
+     So the Go profile names this file, and nothing else does. The grid stays
+     Go's 4 by 4: four applications in four columns is what this layout wants,
+     and the icon size for a 1072 by 1448 panel is a separate question with its
+     own measurements.
+
+     Editing this file is half a change. A database that exists is never seeded
+     again at the same version, so SCHEMA_VERSION in LauncherProvider.java
+     moves with every edit here, or the edit reaches nobody who already has the
+     system. That is what happened to 0010 and then, from the other side, to
+     0011.
+
+     Row 0 of the first screen is the search box (0004), so the applications
+     start at row 1, in the order they are reached for: read, then the web,
+     then what is stored, then settings.
+
+     The first of them is WeRead before WeRead is installed: the installer own
+     entry (WeReadInstaller/StatusActivity), under WeRead name and an icon
+     that says it is a download. Without it nothing on this device says that
+     WeRead can be had here at all. It takes itself off once WeRead is
+     installed, and WeRead own icon is placed in the cell it leaves. -->
+<favorites xmlns:launcher="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto/com.android.launcher3">
+
+    <favorite
+        launcher:screen="0"
+        launcher:x="0"
+        launcher:y="1"
+        launcher:packageName="org.readom.wereadinstaller"
+        launcher:className="org.readom.wereadinstaller.StatusActivity" />
+
+    <favorite
+        launcher:screen="0"
+        launcher:x="1"
+        launcher:y="1"
+        launcher:packageName="info.plateaukao.einkbro"
+        launcher:className="info.plateaukao.einkbro.activity.BrowserActivity" />
+
+    <favorite
+        launcher:screen="0"
+        launcher:x="2"
+        launcher:y="1"
+        launcher:packageName="com.android.documentsui"
+        launcher:className="com.android.documentsui.LauncherActivity" />
+
+    <favorite
+        launcher:screen="0"
+        launcher:x="3"
+        launcher:y="1"
+        launcher:packageName="com.android.settings"
+        launcher:className="com.android.settings.Settings" />
+
+</favorites>
diff --git a/src/com/android/launcher3/LauncherProvider.java b/src/com/android/launcher3/LauncherProvider.java
index 0e387c4..823b719 100644
--- a/src/com/android/launcher3/LauncherProvider.java
+++ b/src/com/android/launcher3/LauncherProvider.java
@@ -85,10 +85,12 @@ public class LauncherProvider extends ContentProvider {
     /**
      * Represents the schema of the database. Changes in scheme need not be backwards compatible.
      */
-    /* PW3: 28 because the default home screen changed. The version is what
+    /* PW3: 29 because the default home screen changed. The version is what
      * decides whether a workspace seeded by an older release is carried
-     * forward or seeded again (onUpgrade below). */
-    public static final int SCHEMA_VERSION = 28;
+     * forward or seeded again (onUpgrade below), and it moves in every release
+     * that changes what the first open of the home screen shows: the layout
+     * file, and the profile entry that names it. */
+    public static final int SCHEMA_VERSION = 29;
 
     public static final String AUTHORITY = (BuildConfig.APPLICATION_ID + ".settings").intern();
 
@@ -844,6 +846,15 @@ public class LauncherProvider extends ContentProvider {
                     // in a release that changes the default layout.
                     break;
                 case 28:
+                    // PW3: 28 seeded the workspace again and seeded it from the
+                    // wrong file: the layout was in default_workspace_5x6.xml
+                    // and the image reads what the Go profile names, which was
+                    // AOSP's 4x4 layout and its phone hotseat. That is why the
+                    // home screen it produced held a browser alone. Now that
+                    // the profile names this project's layout, the workspace is
+                    // worth seeding once more, for the same reason 27 was.
+                    break;
+                case 29:
                     // DB Upgraded successfully
                     return;
             }
